<dashboard version="1.1" theme="dark">
  <label>Configure Trellix ePO Add-on</label>
  <description>Configure connection settings for Trellix (McAfee) ePO server</description>
  
  <row>
    <html>
      <style>
        .setup-container { 
          max-width: 800px; 
          margin: 0 auto; 
          padding: 20px;
          font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;
        }
        .setup-section {
          background: #21262d;
          border: 1px solid #30363d;
          border-radius: 12px;
          padding: 24px;
          margin-bottom: 20px;
        }
        .setup-section h2 {
          color: #58a6ff;
          margin-top: 0;
          padding-bottom: 12px;
          border-bottom: 1px solid #30363d;
          font-size: 1.3em;
        }
        .setup-section h3 {
          color: #c9d1d9;
          margin-top: 16px;
          font-size: 1.1em;
        }
        .info-box {
          background: #0d1117;
          border-left: 4px solid #238636;
          padding: 16px;
          margin: 16px 0;
          border-radius: 4px;
        }
        .warning-box {
          background: #0d1117;
          border-left: 4px solid #d29922;
          padding: 16px;
          margin: 16px 0;
          border-radius: 4px;
        }
        .code-block {
          background: #161b22;
          border: 1px solid #30363d;
          border-radius: 6px;
          padding: 12px 16px;
          font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace;
          font-size: 13px;
          overflow-x: auto;
          margin: 12px 0;
          color: #79c0ff;
        }
        .step-list {
          counter-reset: steps;
          list-style: none;
          padding-left: 0;
        }
        .step-list li {
          counter-increment: steps;
          padding: 12px 0 12px 48px;
          position: relative;
          border-bottom: 1px solid #21262d;
        }
        .step-list li:before {
          content: counter(steps);
          position: absolute;
          left: 0;
          top: 12px;
          width: 28px;
          height: 28px;
          background: #238636;
          border-radius: 50%;
          text-align: center;
          line-height: 28px;
          font-weight: bold;
          color: white;
        }
        .btn-primary {
          background: #238636;
          color: white;
          border: none;
          padding: 10px 20px;
          border-radius: 6px;
          cursor: pointer;
          font-size: 14px;
          margin: 8px 8px 8px 0;
        }
        .btn-primary:hover {
          background: #2ea043;
        }
        .btn-secondary {
          background: #21262d;
          color: #c9d1d9;
          border: 1px solid #30363d;
          padding: 10px 20px;
          border-radius: 6px;
          cursor: pointer;
          font-size: 14px;
          margin: 8px 8px 8px 0;
        }
        .config-table {
          width: 100%;
          border-collapse: collapse;
          margin: 16px 0;
        }
        .config-table th, .config-table td {
          padding: 12px;
          text-align: left;
          border-bottom: 1px solid #30363d;
        }
        .config-table th {
          background: #161b22;
          color: #58a6ff;
          font-weight: 600;
        }
      </style>
      
      <div class="setup-container">
        
        <div class="setup-section">
          <h2>🔧 Configuration Overview</h2>
          <p>This add-on requires configuration to connect to your Trellix (McAfee) ePO server. Follow the steps below to complete the setup.</p>
          
          <div class="info-box">
            <strong>ℹ️ Configuration Files Location:</strong><br/>
            Settings are stored in <code>$SPLUNK_HOME/etc/apps/TA-trellix-epo/local/</code>
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="setup-section">
          <h2>📋 Step 1: Configure ePO Server Settings</h2>
          <p>Edit the settings configuration file to specify your ePO server details:</p>
          
          <h3>Create/Edit Configuration File</h3>
          <div class="code-block">
# Copy template to local directory<br/>
cp $SPLUNK_HOME/etc/apps/TA-trellix-epo/default/ta_trellix_epo_settings.conf \<br/>
   $SPLUNK_HOME/etc/apps/TA-trellix-epo/local/ta_trellix_epo_settings.conf
          </div>
          
          <h3>Edit the [general] Section</h3>
          <div class="code-block">
[general]<br/>
epo_server = your-epo-server.company.com<br/>
epo_port = 8443<br/>
username = your_epo_username<br/>
use_ssl = 1<br/>
verify_ssl = 1<br/>
polling_interval = 300<br/>
batch_size = 1000<br/>
timeout = 30<br/>
retry_attempts = 3<br/>
log_level = INFO
          </div>
          
          <table class="config-table">
            <tr><th>Setting</th><th>Description</th><th>Default</th></tr>
            <tr><td>epo_server</td><td>ePO server hostname or IP address</td><td>(required)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>epo_port</td><td>ePO server port</td><td>8443</td></tr>
            <tr><td>username</td><td>ePO API username</td><td>(required)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>use_ssl</td><td>Enable SSL/TLS (1=yes, 0=no)</td><td>1</td></tr>
            <tr><td>verify_ssl</td><td>Verify SSL certificate (1=yes, 0=no)</td><td>1</td></tr>
            <tr><td>polling_interval</td><td>Default data collection interval (seconds)</td><td>300</td></tr>
            <tr><td>batch_size</td><td>Number of records per API call</td><td>1000</td></tr>
            <tr><td>timeout</td><td>API request timeout (seconds)</td><td>30</td></tr>
            <tr><td>retry_attempts</td><td>Number of retry attempts on failure</td><td>3</td></tr>
            <tr><td>log_level</td><td>Logging level (DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR)</td><td>INFO</td></tr>
          </table>
        </div>
        
        <div class="setup-section">
          <h2>🔐 Step 2: Configure Password Securely</h2>
          <p>Store your ePO password securely using Splunk's encrypted credential storage:</p>
          
          <div class="warning-box">
            <strong>⚠️ Important:</strong> Never store passwords in plain text configuration files. Use the secure credential storage method below.
          </div>
          
          <h3>Run the Credential Configuration Script</h3>
          <div class="code-block">
# Windows<br/>
cd %SPLUNK_HOME%\bin<br/>
splunk cmd python ..\etc\apps\TA-trellix-epo\bin\configure_credentials.py<br/>
<br/>
# Linux/Mac<br/>
cd $SPLUNK_HOME/bin<br/>
./splunk cmd python ../etc/apps/TA-trellix-epo/bin/configure_credentials.py
          </div>
          
          <p>The script will prompt you to enter:</p>
          <ol class="step-list">
            <li>Your ePO username (must match the username in settings)</li>
            <li>Your ePO password (input will be hidden)</li>
            <li>Confirm the password</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
        
        <div class="setup-section">
          <h2>📥 Step 3: Enable Data Inputs</h2>
          <p>Configure which data sources to collect from ePO:</p>
          
          <h3>Create Local Inputs Configuration</h3>
          <div class="code-block">
# Copy template to local directory<br/>
cp $SPLUNK_HOME/etc/apps/TA-trellix-epo/default/inputs.conf \<br/>
   $SPLUNK_HOME/etc/apps/TA-trellix-epo/local/inputs.conf
          </div>
          
          <h3>Enable Desired Inputs</h3>
          <p>Edit <code>local/inputs.conf</code> and change <code>disabled = 1</code> to <code>disabled = 0</code> for the inputs you want to enable:</p>
          
          <div class="code-block">
[trellix_epo://threat_events]<br/>
disabled = 0<br/>
interval = 300<br/>
index = main<br/>
<br/>
[trellix_epo://malware_detections]<br/>
disabled = 0<br/>
interval = 300<br/>
index = main
          </div>
          
          <table class="config-table">
            <tr><th>Input</th><th>Description</th><th>Recommended Interval</th></tr>
            <tr><td>threat_events</td><td>Security threat events and detections</td><td>300s (5 min)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>malware_detections</td><td>Malware detection events</td><td>300s (5 min)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>host_status</td><td>Endpoint protection status</td><td>600s (10 min)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>agent_status</td><td>ePO agent status information</td><td>600s (10 min)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>policy_compliance</td><td>Policy compliance data</td><td>900s (15 min)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>quarantine_events</td><td>Quarantine actions</td><td>300s (5 min)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>user_actions</td><td>ePO user activity logs</td><td>900s (15 min)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>dat_updates</td><td>DAT/signature update status</td><td>3600s (1 hour)</td></tr>
          </table>
        </div>
        
        <div class="setup-section">
          <h2>🔄 Step 4: Restart Splunk</h2>
          <p>After completing the configuration, restart Splunk to apply changes:</p>
          
          <div class="code-block">
# Windows<br/>
%SPLUNK_HOME%\bin\splunk restart<br/>
<br/>
# Linux/Mac<br/>
$SPLUNK_HOME/bin/splunk restart
          </div>
          
          <div class="info-box">
            <strong>✅ Verification:</strong> After restart, check <code>Settings → Data inputs → Trellix ePO</code> to verify your inputs are running.
          </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="setup-section">
          <h2>🔗 Quick Links</h2>
          <p>
            <a href="/manager/TA-trellix-epo/data/inputs/trellix_epo" class="btn-primary">Manage Data Inputs</a>
            <a href="/app/TA-trellix-epo/trellix_epo_overview" class="btn-primary">View Dashboard</a>
            <a href="/app/TA-trellix-epo/search" class="btn-secondary">Search Data</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/sarat1kyan/TA-trellix-epo" target="_blank" class="btn-secondary">Documentation</a>
          </p>
        </div>
        
      </div>
    </html>
  </row>
</dashboard>
